  "id": "yerkesdodson-law",
  "term": "Yerkes–Dodson law",
  "definition": "The Yerkes–Dodson law is the idea that performance tends to be best at a moderate level of stress or arousal. In this pattern, too little or too much stress is linked with poorer productivity and a more negative mood.",
